# BUGS

No link training, PHY programming, mode setting, MST, audio, PSR or HDCP: a transmitter firmware didn't enable stays dark.
An HPD event's sink is read on the interrupt's thread, which waits for each AUX reply, up to 10 ms each, and for a sink just plugged up to 500 ms more.
That the core clears `INTERRUPT_CAUSE` when it is read is presumed, not documented.
